---
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
import '../styles/panels.css';
import '../styles/hud.css';
import '../styles/animations.css';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>QUANTUM GUIDE | Interactive Principles</title>
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
</head>
<body>
  <Navbar activePage="tutorial" />

  <main class="tutorial-container">
    <div class="tutorial-header">
      <span class="quantum-badge badge-cyan">QUANTUM GUIDE</span>
      <h1>How the quantum part works</h1>
      <p class="tutorial-intro">
        Six short modules on the ideas behind Quantum Maze. Each demo runs a real statevector simulation
        right in your browser, so press the buttons and watch the state change.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="modules-stack">
      <!-- 1. Qubit -->
      <section class="glass-panel module-card">
        <div class="module-number">MODULE 01</div>
        <h2 class="module-title">What is a qubit?</h2>
        <div class="module-text">
          <p>
            A classical bit is either <strong>0</strong> or <strong>1</strong>. A quantum bit (<strong>qubit</strong>)
            can be in a superposition of both basis states:
          </p>
          <div class="dirac-formula">|ψ⟩ = α|0⟩ + β|1⟩</div>
          <p>
            α and β are complex amplitudes with <strong>|α|² + |β|² = 1</strong>. When you measure, you get 0 with
            probability |α|² and 1 with probability |β|².
          </p>
          <div class="game-callout">
            <strong>In the game:</strong> every level has a target qubit. The exit only opens once that qubit is
            likely enough (or certain) to read the value the exit asks for.
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Hadamard -->
      <section class="glass-panel module-card">
        <div class="module-number">MODULE 02</div>
        <h2 class="module-title">Superposition and the Hadamard gate (H)</h2>
        <div class="module-text">
          <p>The Hadamard gate turns a basis state into an equal superposition:</p>
          <div class="dirac-formula">H|0⟩ = (|0⟩ + |1⟩) / √2 &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; H|1⟩ = (|0⟩ − |1⟩) / √2</div>
          <p>
            That gives a <strong>50 / 50</strong> chance of measuring 0 or 1. Apply H twice and you are back to |0⟩,
            because H undoes itself.
          </p>
          <div class="game-callout">
            <strong>In the game:</strong> H is the quickest way to move a qubit off 0% toward the exit's target.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tg-demo" data-qubits="1" aria-label="Hadamard demo">
          <div class="tg-head">
            <span class="tg-title">Try it</span>
            <div class="tg-actions">
              <button class="btn-quantum tg-btn" type="button" data-op="H:0">Apply H</button>
              <button class="tg-plain tg-btn" type="button" data-op="reset">Reset</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tg-out"></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. Pauli-X -->
      <section class="glass-panel module-card">
        <div class="module-number">MODULE 03</div>
        <h2 class="module-title">Pauli-X, the quantum NOT</h2>
        <div class="module-text">
          <p>The X gate swaps the two basis states, just like a classical NOT:</p>
          <div class="dirac-formula">X|0⟩ = |1⟩ &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; X|1⟩ = |0⟩</div>
          <div class="game-callout">
            <strong>In the game:</strong> when the exit needs |1⟩ and your qubit is sitting at |0⟩, one X takes it
            straight to 100%.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tg-demo" data-qubits="1" aria-label="Pauli-X demo">
          <div class="tg-head">
            <span class="tg-title">Try it</span>
            <div class="tg-actions">
              <button class="btn-quantum tg-btn" type="button" data-op="X:0">Apply X</button>
              <button class="tg-plain tg-btn" type="button" data-op="reset">Reset</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tg-out"></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. Phase / Z -->
      <section class="glass-panel module-card">
        <div class="module-number">MODULE 04</div>
        <h2 class="module-title">Phase and the Pauli-Z gate</h2>
        <div class="module-text">
          <p>Z leaves |0⟩ alone and flips the sign of |1⟩:</p>
          <div class="dirac-formula">Z|0⟩ = |0⟩ &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; Z|1⟩ = −|1⟩</div>
          <p>
            On its own Z does not change any probability, only the <strong>phase</strong>. But phase decides how
            amplitudes interfere: H, then Z, then H turns |0⟩ into |1⟩ with certainty.
          </p>
          <div class="game-callout">
            <strong>In the game:</strong> watch the phase column. A gate that leaves the exit probability unchanged
            can still set up the next H to land exactly where you need it.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tg-demo" data-qubits="1" aria-label="Phase demo">
          <div class="tg-head">
            <span class="tg-title">Try H, Z, H</span>
            <div class="tg-actions">
              <button class="btn-quantum tg-btn" type="button" data-op="H:0">Apply H</button>
              <button class="btn-quantum tg-btn" type="button" data-op="Z:0">Apply Z</button>
              <button class="tg-plain tg-btn" type="button" data-op="reset">Reset</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tg-out"></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Entanglement -->
      <section class="glass-panel module-card">
        <div class="module-number">MODULE 05</div>
        <h2 class="module-title">Entanglement and CNOT</h2>
        <div class="module-text">
          <p>
            CNOT flips the target qubit only when the control qubit is |1⟩. Put the control in superposition with H
            first, then CNOT, and you get a <strong>Bell state</strong>:
          </p>
          <div class="dirac-formula">|Φ⁺⟩ = (|00⟩ + |11⟩) / √2</div>
          <p>The two qubits now always agree when measured, even though each one alone is a coin flip.</p>
          <div class="game-callout">
            <strong>In the game:</strong> later levels have exits that only open when the target qubit is
            entangled with its partner.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tg-demo" data-qubits="2" aria-label="Bell state demo">
          <div class="tg-head">
            <span class="tg-title">Build a Bell pair</span>
            <div class="tg-actions">
              <button class="btn-quantum tg-btn" type="button" data-op="H:0">H on q0</button>
              <button class="btn-quantum tg-btn" type="button" data-op="CNOT:0:1">CNOT q0 to q1</button>
              <button class="tg-plain tg-btn" type="button" data-op="reset">Reset</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tg-out"></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. Measurement -->
      <section class="glass-panel module-card">
        <div class="module-number">MODULE 06</div>
        <h2 class="module-title">Measurement and collapse</h2>
        <div class="module-text">
          <p>
            Measuring a qubit forces it to pick 0 or 1, with odds given by the Born rule. After that the
            superposition is gone:
          </p>
          <div class="dirac-formula">P(0) = |α|² &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; P(1) = |β|²</div>
          <div class="game-callout">
            <strong>In the game:</strong> measuring costs energy and each level allows only a few. It is a gamble
            unless the odds are already on your side.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tg-demo" data-qubits="1" aria-label="Measurement demo">
          <div class="tg-head">
            <span class="tg-title">Superpose, then measure</span>
            <div class="tg-actions">
              <button class="btn-quantum tg-btn" type="button" data-op="H:0">Apply H</button>
              <button class="btn-quantum tg-btn" type="button" data-op="M:0">Measure</button>
              <button class="tg-plain tg-btn" type="button" data-op="reset">Reset</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tg-out"></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="tutorial-next">
        <a class="btn-quantum" href="/lab?preset=bell">Open the Quantum Lab</a>
        <a class="tg-plain" href="/levels">Play the levels</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <script>
    import { QuantumSim } from '../lib/game/quantumSim';

    const newSeed = () => Math.floor(Math.random() * 1e9) + 1;

    function setupDemo(root: HTMLElement) {
      const n = parseInt(root.dataset.qubits || '1', 10);
      const out = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.tg-out')!;
      let sim = new QuantumSim(n, newSeed());
      let steps: string[] = [];

      function render() {
        const info = sim.stateInfo();
        const rows = info.basis_states
          .map((b) => {
            const pct = b.probability * 100;
            const zero = b.probability < 1e-6;
            return `<div class="tg-row${zero ? ' is-zero' : ''}">
              <span class="tg-ket">|${b.binary}⟩</span>
              <div class="tg-track"><div class="tg-fill" style="width:${pct}%"></div></div>
              <span class="tg-pct">${pct.toFixed(0)}%</span>
              <span class="tg-phase">${zero ? '' : `phase ${Math.round(b.phase_degrees) % 360}°`}</span>
            </div>`;
          })
          .join('');
        const start = `|${'0'.repeat(n)}⟩`;
        out.innerHTML = `
          <div class="tg-steps">${steps.length ? `Steps: ${steps.join(', ')}` : `Starting state ${start}`}</div>
          <div class="dirac-formula tg-state">|ψ⟩ = ${info.dirac_notation}</div>
          ${rows}`;
      }

      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-op]').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const [op, a, b] = (btn.dataset.op || '').split(':');
          if (op === 'reset') {
            sim = new QuantumSim(n, newSeed());
            steps = [];
          } else if (op === 'M') {
            const { outcome } = sim.measure(+a);
            steps.push(`measured ${outcome}`);
          } else if (op === 'CNOT') {
            sim.gate('CNOT', +b, +a);
            steps.push(`CNOT q${a} to q${b}`);
          } else {
            sim.gate(op, +a, null);
            steps.push(n > 1 ? `${op} q${a}` : op);
          }
          render();
        });
      });

      render();
    }

    function init() {
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.tg-demo').forEach(setupDemo);
    }

    if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
    else init();
  </script>

  <style is:global>
    .tutorial-container {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 36px 16px 60px;
    }

    .tutorial-header {
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 32px;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
    }
    .tutorial-header h1 { font-size: clamp(24px, 4vw, 32px); margin: 0; }
    .tutorial-intro { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; max-width: 640px; margin: 0; line-height: 1.6; }

    .modules-stack { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; }
    .module-card { padding: 24px; }

    .module-number {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--accent);
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
    }
    .module-title { font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 14px; }
    .module-text { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--text); }
    .module-text p { margin: 0 0 10px; }
    .module-text .dirac-formula { margin: 12px 0; }

    .game-callout {
      background: var(--bg);
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
      padding: 10px 14px;
      border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;
      margin-top: 12px;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .tg-demo {
      margin-top: 16px;
      background: var(--bg);
      border: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 4px;
      padding: 14px;
    }
    .tg-head {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }
    .tg-title { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
    .tg-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; }
    .tg-btn { padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 12px; }

    .tg-plain {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--text);
      background: var(--panel-2, var(--bg));
      border: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 4px;
      padding: 6px 12px;
      cursor: pointer;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .tg-plain:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }

    .tg-steps { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
    .tg-state { margin: 0 0 10px; word-break: break-word; }
    .tg-row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 44px minmax(40px, 1fr) 44px 84px;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12px;
      margin-top: 6px;
    }
    .tg-row.is-zero { opacity: 0.45; }
    .tg-ket { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; }
    .tg-track { height: 12px; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 2px; overflow: hidden; }
    .tg-fill { height: 100%; background: var(--accent); transition: width 0.25s ease; }
    .tg-pct { text-align: right; }
    .tg-phase { color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; }

    .tutorial-next { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 10px; margin-top: 8px; }
    .tutorial-next a { text-decoration: none; padding: 10px 18px; font-size: 13px; }

    @media (max-width: 480px) {
      .module-card { padding: 16px; }
      .tg-row { grid-template-columns: 40px minmax(30px, 1fr) 40px; }
      .tg-phase { display: none; }
    }
  </style>
</body>
</html>
